workedExamples.solution_text:
The curve is positive throughout the interval. The shaded region represents the required area.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=35mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{areaBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[areaBlue] (-4,0) -- plot[domain=-4:6.928203,samples=100] (\x,{8/(16+(\x)*(\x))}) -- (6.928203,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->,black] (-5,0)--(8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,0.65) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-5:8,samples=120] (\x,{8/(16+(\x)*(\x))});
\draw[black] (-4,0)--(-4,0.25);
\draw[black] (6.928203,0)--(6.928203,0.125);
\path (-4,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-4$} (6.928203,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$4\sqrt{3}$} (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$} (3,0.52) node[right] {$y=\frac{8}{16+x^{2}}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}A&=\int_{-4}^{4\sqrt{3}}\frac{8}{16+x^{2}}\,dx\\&=\left[2\arctan\frac{x}{4}\right]_{-4}^{4\sqrt{3}}\\&=2\arctan\sqrt{3}-2\arctan(-1)\\&=\frac{2\pi}{3}+\frac{\pi}{2}\\&=\frac{7\pi}{6}\end{aligned}$
The area is $\frac{7\pi}{6}$ square units.

