Find the exact area of the shaded region bounded by $y=\dfrac{6}{4+x^{2}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=-2$ and $x=2\sqrt{3}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4.5, xmax=5.5, ymin=0, ymax=2, samples=120, width=11cm, height=7cm, xtick={-2,3.4641}, xticklabels={$-2$,$2\sqrt{3}$}, ytick={1.5}, yticklabels={$1.5$}, every tick label/.style={font=\small}]
\addplot[draw=none, fill=gray!35, domain=-2:3.4641] {6/(4+x*x)} \closedcycle;
\addplot[thick, domain=-4.5:5.5] {6/(4+x*x)};
\node[anchor=west] at (axis cs:2.2,1.6) {$y=\frac{6}{4+x^{2}}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
